{
 "note": "Verdicts for the Jena ARQ expression cases that do not meet the Jena expectation on @factoidal/core. \"defect\": Factoidal differs from the specification (expected failure, names an open issue). \"divergence\": a Jena extension, or Jena differs from the specification. Each group cites the specification. Measured 2026-10-26 on @factoidal/core 0.16.0 (wasm from core 0069da82e).",
 "groups": {
  "string-arg-types-1036": {
   "class": "defect",
   "issue": "https://github.com/danbri/factoidal/issues/1036",
   "spec": "SPARQL 1.1 §17.4.3.1.1, §17.4.3.1.2 (SPARQL 1.2 WD 2026-10-25 §17.4.3): a string function takes a string literal; §17.4.3.1.4 argument compatibility; SPARQL 1.1 §17.4.6 (SPARQL 1.2 WD 2026-10-25 §17.4.7): MD5/SHA* take xsd:string",
   "gloss": "a number, IRI or incompatible language tag is accepted; fixed by https://github.com/danbri/factoidal-core/pull/126 (measured: native l4factoidal built from its head 7053f548 meets the Jena expectation in all 44 cases of the two 1036 groups, and in no other case)"
  },
  "substr-fn-substring-1036": {
   "class": "defect",
   "issue": "https://github.com/danbri/factoidal/issues/1036",
   "spec": "SPARQL 1.1 §17.4.3.3 (SPARQL 1.2 WD 2026-10-25 §17.4.3.2) SUBSTR is XPath fn:substring (F&O 3.1 §5.4.3): positions p with start <= p < start + length, from 1",
   "gloss": "a start below 1 or a negative length is clamped or refused; fixed by https://github.com/danbri/factoidal-core/pull/126 (measured: native l4factoidal built from its head 7053f548 meets the Jena expectation in all 44 cases of the two 1036 groups, and in no other case)"
  },
  "dir-lang-string-functions": {
   "class": "defect",
   "issue": "https://github.com/danbri/factoidal/issues/1042",
   "spec": "SPARQL 1.2 WD 2026-10-25 §17.4.3 (argument compatible: same language tag and same base direction; result of the same kind as the first argument), §17.4.3.8 STRBEFORE, §17.4.3.9 STRAFTER",
   "gloss": "the base direction of an rdf:dirLangString is ignored or dropped"
  },
  "xsd-constructor-relabels": {
   "class": "defect",
   "issue": "https://github.com/danbri/factoidal/issues/1041",
   "spec": "SPARQL 1.1 §17.5 (SPARQL 1.2 WD 2026-10-25 §17.5) constructor functions are the XPath F&O 3.1 §19 casts: FORG0001 outside the value space, XPTY0004 for a cast the table does not allow",
   "gloss": "the constructor keeps the lexical form and changes only the datatype, so the result is ill-typed"
  },
  "iriref-digit-573": {
   "class": "defect",
   "issue": "https://github.com/danbri/factoidal/issues/573",
   "spec": "SPARQL 1.1 §19.8 [139] IRIREF (SPARQL 1.2 WD 2026-10-25 §19.7): a digit can follow \"<\"",
   "gloss": "the SPARQL lexer refuses <123> (the Lean engine has the defect of the F* parser in the issue)"
  },
  "ext-function-iri": {
   "class": "divergence",
   "spec": "SPARQL 1.1 §17.6 (SPARQL 1.2 WD 2026-10-25 §17.6): a function IRI that the processor does not support is an error; afn:, lfn:, math:, fn:numeric-*, op:*, sparql:* are not SPARQL functions",
   "gloss": "Jena extension function"
  },
  "ext-syntax": {
   "class": "divergence",
   "spec": "SPARQL 1.1 §19.8 grammar (SPARQL 1.2 WD 2026-10-25 §19.7): IDIV, MOD, \"idiv\"/\"mod\" infix, EBV(), CALL() and sameValue() are not SPARQL syntax; SPARQL 1.2 WD 2026-10-25 §17.4.2.2: sameValue \"cannot be used directly in expressions\"",
   "gloss": "Jena (ARQ) syntax extension"
  },
  "datetime-accessors": {
   "class": "divergence",
   "spec": "SPARQL 1.1 §17.4.5.2-§17.4.5.7 (SPARQL 1.2 WD 2026-10-25 same): YEAR, MONTH, DAY, HOURS, MINUTES, SECONDS take xsd:dateTime only",
   "gloss": "Jena accepts xsd:date, xsd:time, xsd:g* and xsd:duration"
  },
  "operator-table": {
   "class": "divergence",
   "spec": "SPARQL 1.1 §17.3 (SPARQL 1.2 WD 2026-10-25 §17.3): <, >, <=, >= are defined for numerics, strings, booleans and xsd:dateTime only; other operands are a type error; §17.3.1 allows extensions",
   "gloss": "Jena orders xsd:time, xsd:dateTimeStamp, xsd:gYear and durations"
  },
  "equality-of-other-terms": {
   "class": "divergence",
   "spec": "SPARQL 1.1 §17.4.1.7 RDFterm-equal: two literals that are not the same term, with no operator in §17.3, give a type error; SPARQL 1.2 WD 2026-10-25 §17.4.2.2 sameValue: true or false only where the processor can determine the values, otherwise an error",
   "gloss": "Jena gives true/false; Factoidal gives the SPARQL 1.1 error (SPARQL 1.2 leaves this to the processor)"
  },
  "lexical-form": {
   "class": "divergence",
   "spec": "SPARQL 1.1 §17.1: a function result is a typed value mapped back to a literal; SPARQL does not fix its lexical form (XSD 1.1 Part 2 §3.3 gives canonical forms)",
   "gloss": "same value and datatype, other lexical form (Jena keeps the input form or writes \"1.0e0\")"
  },
  "cast-double-to-decimal": {
   "class": "divergence",
   "spec": "XPath F&O 3.1 §19.1.2.3: xs:double to xs:decimal is the xs:decimal value numerically closest to the double",
   "gloss": "Factoidal gives the exact value of the binary double; Jena rounds to the shortest decimal"
  },
  "cast-whitespace": {
   "class": "divergence",
   "spec": "XPath F&O 3.1 §19.2: whitespace normalization (the whiteSpace facet) is applied before the lexical check",
   "gloss": "Jena refuses \" 1\"; F&O casts it"
  },
  "cast-date-to-datetime": {
   "class": "divergence",
   "spec": "SPARQL 1.1 §17.5 (SPARQL 1.2 WD 2026-10-25 §17.5): xsd:dateTime casts from xsd:string and xsd:dateTime only; F&O 3.1 §19.1 also allows xs:date",
   "gloss": "Jena extension beyond the SPARQL casting table"
  },
  "replace-empty-match": {
   "class": "divergence",
   "spec": "SPARQL 1.1 §17.4.3.15 (SPARQL 1.2 WD 2026-10-25 §17.4.3.13) REPLACE is fn:replace; XPath F&O 3.1 §5.6.4: error FORX0003 when the pattern matches the empty string",
   "gloss": "Jena (Java regex) replaces empty matches"
  },
  "iri-of-blank-node": {
   "class": "divergence",
   "spec": "SPARQL 1.1 §17.4.2.8 (SPARQL 1.2 WD 2026-10-25 §17.4.2.13) IRI takes an IRI, a simple literal or an xsd:string; a blank node is a type error",
   "gloss": "Jena gives an IRI for IRI(BNODE())"
  },
  "lang-tag-case": {
   "class": "divergence",
   "spec": "RDF 1.1 Concepts §3.3: lexical forms of language tags MAY be converted to lower case",
   "gloss": "Jena writes the BCP 47 case (en-GB)"
  },
  "plus-on-strings": {
   "class": "divergence",
   "spec": "SPARQL 1.1 §17.3 (SPARQL 1.2 WD 2026-10-25 §17.3): \"+\" is defined for numerics only",
   "gloss": "Jena concatenates strings with +"
  },
  "substr-non-integer": {
   "class": "divergence",
   "spec": "SPARQL 1.1 §17.4.3.3 (SPARQL 1.2 WD 2026-10-25 §17.4.3.2): SUBSTR(string literal, xsd:integer, xsd:integer); another type is an error",
   "gloss": "Jena takes doubles and rounds them (F&O fn:substring). Note: Factoidal 0.16.0 gives \"12345\" for SUBSTR(\"12345\", 1, NaN); https://github.com/danbri/factoidal-core/pull/126 makes it an error"
  }
 },
